<!--
  MLIE_FAUNA_ABSORPTION_1 Wave C — Beldon creature port.
  Ported from mlie.starwarsanimalcollection's `Beldon` ThingDef/PawnKindDef
  pair (Races_Animal_SW.xml, workshop folder 3497316713), renamed under the
  RSW_ tier prefix. Geometry/stats/comps copied verbatim. The most
  dependency-heavy species this wave: a flying, tentacled gasbag needing 4
  things no prior Wave C species needed:
    1. A custom BodyDef (`Beldon` -> RSW_Beldon, RSW_MlieWaveC_Bodies.xml)
       whose 3 tentacle parts reuse Wave B's already-ported body-part-groups
       (RSW_SW_FirstTentacleBeldon/SecondTentacleBeldon/ThirdTentacleBeldon,
       RSW_SWTentacleAttackTool) and BodyPartDefs (RSW_SW_LeftTentacle/
       RSW_SW_RightTentacle/RSW_SW_DorsalTentacle) — no new body part needed.
    2. A custom PawnRenderTreeDef (`Beldon` -> RSW_Beldon,
       RSW_MlieWaveC_RenderTree.xml, MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Anomaly")
       drawing the 3 tentacles via vanilla Anomaly's own
       `PawnRenderNodeProperties_BulbfreakTentacle` node class (Mlie ships
       0 C#, so this is a vanilla Anomaly render-node type, not donor code) —
       texPaths point at the same extracted Textures/swanimals/Beldon/Tentacles/
       files the BodyDef's groups attach to.
    3. Its Odyssey ability (SW_SootheSong) had no prior-wave port — new
       AbilityDef/HediffDef/TrainableDef trio, RSW_SW_SootheSong
       (RSW_MlieWaveC_Abilities.xml). Its soundCast repoints to the
       already-absorbed RSW_Ability_SootheSong (2026-09-02 sound wave). Its
       HediffDef's RecoveryThought (`SoothingSong`) is donor content too —
       ported as RSW_SoothingSong (RSW_Bantha_Thoughts.xml, alongside
       RSW_AteMudhornEgg).
    4. Two new eggs (RSW_MlieWaveC_Resources.xml): RSW_EggBeldonFertilized/
       UnFertilized, texPath swresource/EggSpore (newly extracted this pass,
       not reused from an earlier wave).
  `specificMeatDef` repoints to newly-ported RSW_Silica_Meat
  (RSW_MlieWaveC_Resources.xml, texPath swresource/Meat_Silica, newly
  extracted). `bloodDef` (Filth_Slime) and `milkDef` (Chemfuel, via
  CompProperties_Milkable) are vanilla Core — left unprefixed, unchanged.
  `deathAction` (DeathActionWorker_BigExplosion) is a vanilla RimWorld
  worker class. Art: extracted via extract_bundle.py from the same
  AssetBundle every prior wave used — of the donor's 64 Beldon-matching
  textures, only the 28 this ThingDef/PawnKindDef/RenderTreeDef trio
  actually reference were kept (base Beldon/BeldonC east/north/south,
  Beldon_Dessicated, the 3x3 Beldon_Flying_*/BeldonC_Flying_* animation
  frames, 3 tentacle textures); the BeldonA/BeldonB/BeldonW color-variant
  textures are unreferenced by any def here and were left unextracted, same
  as the Wave B AcklayW/DewbackPack unused-variant call.

  Wired into the live cast this same pass: AridShrubland/Desert/ExtremeDesert
  all at 0.01 (donor's own wildBiomes weight — Beldon is a rare exotic
  everywhere in the donor's own design, not just here), repointed from the
  bare "Beldon" entry in cast_assignment.csv / BiomeCast_Ashkarr.xml.
-->
<Defs>
<ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase" ADogSaidBody="LegsTail">
    <defName>RSW_Beldon</defName>
    <label>beldon</label>
    <description>Beldons were a large cnidaria species native to the gas giant Bespin. They lived in the planet's lower atmosphere and could be found in large herds. They used the long tendrils on their bodies to gather atmospheric plankton and chemicals and so require very little direct nutrition. This variety appears to have been engineered to not only survive away from Bespin, but create useful Chemfuel and are thus very combustible.</description>
